# AllTech website — start here

Astro 5 (static-first) + Tailwind v4 + React 18 islands, deployed to a
**Cloudflare Worker with a static-assets binding** (not Cloudflare Pages).
Full context lives in the docs below — read them before making changes; don't
duplicate their content into new files.

## Read these first, in order

1. `README.md` — stack, local dev, the three-way env-var split, deploy model.
2. `LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md` — ordered runbook for cutting `askalltech.com` over
   from the old WordPress site. Some items are still open.
3. `claude.md` — the GEO/SEO instruction set, whose **§7 "Deployment Reality
   Addendum"** documents every place its literal instructions would have broken
   something on this specific codebase. §7 supersedes the earlier sections.
4. `ARCHITECTURE.md` — deeper reference on structure and the contact/assessment
   endpoints.

## Local dev

```bash
npm install
npm run dev        # Astro dev server on http://localhost:4321
```

To exercise the `/api/contact` and `/api/assessment` SSR endpoints against the
real Workers runtime: `npm run build && npm run preview` (`wrangler dev`).
`npm run typecheck` runs `astro check`. Package manager is npm; `.npmrc` pins
`legacy-peer-deps=true`, so keep using npm and the committed `package-lock.json`.

## Non-negotiables (each has already caused a real bug)

- **Env vars live in three different places by *when* they're read** — see the
  table in `README.md` → "Environment variables". Build-time `PUBLIC_*` (baked
  in by Vite at `astro build`), runtime **secrets** (`RESEND_API_KEY`,
  `TURNSTILE_SECRET`, read via `locals.runtime.env`), and runtime **plain vars**
  (`CONTACT_FROM`, `CONTACT_FORWARD_TO`, `ASSESSMENT_FORWARD_TO`). Plain vars
  MUST stay in `wrangler.toml` `[vars]`: Workers Builds redeploys from git on
  every push and wipes any plain var set only in the dashboard. Never put a
  secret in `wrangler.toml` — it's committed to git.
- **Turnstile fails closed when half-configured** — see `src/lib/turnstile.ts`.
  If `PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` is set but `TURNSTILE_SECRET` isn't, the form
  endpoints refuse submissions rather than accept unverified ones. With neither
  set (normal local dev) verification is skipped so forms stay usable. Set both
  or neither.
- **`robots.txt` is host-aware and generated per-request** — see
  `src/pages/robots.txt.ts` (not a static file). Production gets the real
  policy; any non-production host (e.g. `development-preview.askalltech.com`)
  gets a blanket `Disallow: /`. The named AI-crawler group intentionally repeats
  the `Disallow` lines because a named `User-agent` group does not inherit
  `User-agent: *` rules.
- **Deliberate `noindex` pages** — the retired-product pages
  `src/pages/services/home-phone.astro` and
  `src/pages/services/internet-service-alltech-fiber.astro` carry `noindex` on
  purpose and return 410 rather than redirecting. Don't "fix" them into
  redirects. Legal templates under `/legal/` and the 404 page are also `noindex`
  by design.

## Design system

Colors, spacing, radii, shadows are defined once in `src/styles/global.css`
(AllTech tokens + a shadcn bridge). Reference the semantic tokens; don't
hardcode hex values or one-off Tailwind color utilities in a page. See
`README.md` → "Design system" for the token layers and the shadcnblocks caveats.
